%% S1CAP lane view - the five layers, top to bottom, aligned and equal width.
%%
%% Mermaid block layout (`block-beta`, one column): every lane is stretched to the same width, which a
%% flowchart cannot guarantee. Each lane states what it sends and receives, so the picture stays honest
%% without labelled arrows.
%%
%% Arrow-level topology (including the inner loop's self-edge and the asynchronous edges) lives in
%% docs/figures/s1cap-technical-route.html and in the connection table of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §2.
%%
%% Reading order: L1 harness loop -> L2 one System-2 step -> L3 the S1CAP hook (assembler + gate)
%% -> L4 asynchronous graph upkeep -> L5 the System-1 backends. Stopping belongs to the model, so no
%% S1CAP edge can keep the loop alive.
block-beta
  columns 1
  L1["① Harness session — one user turn = many LLM steps<br/>sends session events · act · tool calls — receives the assembled context and the advisory order"]
  L2["② System-2 compute — one LLM step at a time<br/>receives the assembled view (TAS) · sends candidate plans, when the model offers them"]
  L3["③ S1CAP control — per-call hook, advisory<br/>ASSEMBLER (BFS τ,d + budget + TAS) · PLAN GATE (order · attempt cap M = 2)"]
  L4["④ Async RG upkeep — off the critical path<br/>Segment / Recall → RG Upkeep → Association Graph · silent, may lag the session"]
  L5["⑤ System-1 backends — POST /v1/systemone<br/>S1 assoc (noul relevance) · S1 decide (choice scoring) · Laya or Jev runtime"]
